    "A": "Research a generic node-ID index to replace repeated linear `find_by_id` scans. Support arbitrary IDs and preserve first-match behavior if duplicates are admitted; ignore missing neighbor IDs as the source does. Preserve neighbor order (it affects ties) and the original query-token spelling and order in output. Measure whole-program runtime, not just lookup time.",
